---
title: Dutch Baby Pancake (NYT)
prepTime: 5 min
cookTime: 25 min
totalTime: 30 min
rating: 5
description: "This large, fluffy pancake is excellent for breakfast, brunch, lunch and dessert any time of year. And it comes together in about five blessed minutes. Just dump all of the ingredients into a blender, give it a good whirl, pour it into a heated skillet sizzling with butter, and pop it into the oven. Twenty-five minutes later? Bliss. It's wonderful simply with sugar, syrup or preserves, but you also can serve it with fresh berries and whipped cream, apple slices cooked in butter and sugar or banana slices lightly cooked then dusted with brown sugar."
source.name: New York Times
source.url: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/6648-dutch-baby
tags: Breakfast
---

= Pancake =

Place a #heavy 10-inch skillet{} in the oven and heat to 425°F.

In a #small bowl{}, combine the @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}, @sugar{1%tbsp},
@cinnamon{1/4%tsp}, and @nutmeg{1/4%tsp}(fresh grated). 

In a #large bowl{}, whisk the @eggs{3}(large, at room temperature) and @whole milk{1/2%cup}(at room temperature).
Whisk in the dry ingredients until very smooth or use a blender.

When the oven has finished preheating, remove the pan and swirl @butter{4%tbsp}(unsalted, cubed) around the pan until it is melted.
Immediately add the batter to the pan, then return pan to the oven.

Bake for ~{15-20%minutes}, until the pancake is puffed and golden.
Lower oven temperature to 300°F and bake ~{5%min} longer.

= Serving =

Remove pancake from oven, cut into wedges and serve at once.

Optionally top with @maple syrup{}, @fruit preserves{}, @powdered sugar{}, or @cinnamon sugar{}.
